WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.290
“What is your name?” is a question most frequently asked when people meet for the first time.
“你叫什么名字？”是人们初次见面时最常问的问题。

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:12.560
But for me, it was the first challenge I encountered as an international student in Ireland.
可对我来说，这却是我作为留学生在爱尔兰遇到的第一个挑战。

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.110
The pronunciation system of the Chinese language is quite different from that of English.
汉语的发音体系和英语的大不相同。

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.730
For native speakers of English, some Chinese words are rather difficult to pronounce.
对以英语为母语的人来说，有些汉语词语相当难念。

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:29.600
My given name Qiuyu, for instance, happened to be a great challenge for many of them.
比如，我的名字“秋雨”对他们中的许多人来说就恰好是个大难题。

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:38.880
Every time I gave a self-introduction, I had to explain how to pronounce my name at least five times, yet they still could not say it the way I did.
每次做自我介绍，我都得至少解释五遍我的名字怎么念，可他们还是念不成我念的那样。

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:46.300
Once in a lecture, the professor tried repeating my name after me over and over in front of thirty classmates.
有一次上课，教授当着三十个同学的面，跟着我一遍又一遍地念我的名字。

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:51.900
I really did not know whether I should continue correcting him or simply drop the matter.
我真不知道是该继续纠正他，还是干脆就此作罢。

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.390
I feared that my classmates might grow tired of my efforts or even lose patience with me.
我担心同学们会对我的努力感到厌烦，甚至对我失去耐心。

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.560
After all, I did care about what others would think of me.
毕竟，我确实在意别人会怎么看我。

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.120
I realized that if I didn’t stop, the entire lecture would be ruined.
我意识到，要是我不停下来，整堂课都会被毁掉。

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.230
“It’s okay, professor,” I shrugged.
“没关系，教授。”我耸了耸肩。

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.490
The awkward moment ended with the class erupting into laughter.
尴尬的一幕以全班哄堂大笑告终。

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:17.370
I forced a smile, unsure how to respond further.
我勉强挤出一个笑容，不知道该再怎么回应。

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:21.730
After that incident, I stopped acting as a “Chinese teacher.”
那件事以后，我不再充当“汉语老师”了。

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:28.570
Instead of correcting others when they were struggling to pronounce my name, I just smiled and nodded approvingly.
别人费力地念我的名字时，我不再去纠正，只是笑着点头，表示赞许。

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.980
This approach spared me the discomfort of having to over-explain.
这种做法让我免去了不得不过多解释的难堪。

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:42.170
However, I soon found that by doing so, I might be losing something more important: the opportunity to share a small part of my cultural identity.
然而，我很快发现，这样做可能会让我失去某种更重要的东西：分享自己文化身份中一小部分的机会。

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:46.840
In a class discussion, I was invited to explain the meaning of my name.
在一次课堂讨论中，我受邀解释自己名字的含义。

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:51.370
Many of my classmates got interested and came up to me after class.
许多同学产生了兴趣，下课后都来找我。
